{meta: title Where Is My Wandering Boy Tonight}
{meta: x_lyrics_source bluegrass-lyrics}
{meta: x_lyrics_url https://www.bluegrasslyrics.com/song/where-is-my-wandering-boy-tonight/}

{start_of_verse}
Where is my wandering boy tonight
The boy of my tenderest care
The boy that was once my joy and light
The child of my love and prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Where is my boy tonight
Where is my boy tonight
My heart o’erflows for I love him he knows
Oh where is my boy tonight
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
Once he was pure as morning dew
As he knelt at his mother’s knee
No face was so bright no heart more true
And none was so sweet as he
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Oh chould I see you now my boy
As fair as in olden time
When prattle and smile made home a joy
And life was a merry chime
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Go for my wand’ring boy tonight
Go search for him where you will
But bring him to me with all his blight
And tell him I love him still
{end_of_verse}

